@title STORY • SHANE: GENTLE GIANT
@bg beach_sunset
You're Shane Fa'avae. Honolulu, last summer, in your memory. Your whole family on the beach. Your little cousins climbing you like a tree.
Your dad: You're going so far away, son. Who's going to protect them over there?
Shane: Protect who, Dad?
Your dad: Whoever needs it. That's who we are.
@bg campus_quad_night
Present day. 11 p.m. A freshman thrower named Tyrell is sitting alone outside the dorm. Shaking. Phone in his hand.
> [Sweet] Sit down next to him. Don't say anything yet. -> a1
> [Good] "Hey, man. You good?" -> a2
*a1
@add Protector 3
You sit. Five minutes. Then he talks. His mom's sick. He's eight hours from home. He doesn't know anybody.
Shane: You know me now.
@jump a_done
*a2
@add Protector 2
Tyrell: (fast) I'm fine.
Shane: Okay. I'm gonna sit here anyway. My legs are tired.
Your legs aren't tired. He knows. He talks anyway.
*a_done
@bg throws_ring_day
@show coachvega
Coach Vega: Fa'avae. You've got the strongest arm I've coached in ten years and you throw like you're scared to hurt the ball.
Shane: Maybe I am, Coach.
Coach Vega: (laughing) Kid. Being gentle with people is a superpower. Being gentle with a shot put is a waste of a superpower.
> [Bold] Throw it like you mean it. -> b1
> [Sweet] "I don't know how to be two people, Coach." -> b2
*b1
@add Strength 3
It flies. Past the line. Past the cones. Caleb drops his water bottle. Coach Vega takes his hat off.
Coach Vega: There he is. Big Shane. Now go hug somebody, I can see you need it.
You hug Caleb. Caleb wheezes.
@jump end
*b2
@add Strength 2
Coach Vega: You're not two people. You're one big guy who's soft with his friends and strong with his work. Lot of us dads figured that out late. You're early.
You throw a PR on the next attempt. Then you cry a little. Coach Vega pretends not to notice. He's crying too.
*end
Shane Fa'avae is the biggest person on the team and the softest. This year, he learns he doesn't have to choose.
